so in this case we use reverse PROXY 
basicall it will get the request and then indetifies the request whether it should be go 
ex 8080 or 8081 or 8082 

basically it routes the requests

so for that we use nginx
in the AWS machine install --> sudo apt install nginx

go to aws instance and cpoy the url and run it 
here the nginx is running on port 80 

hereafter the nginx will firt receive the request and then forward to the other ports 

for that we need to configure the DNS where we bought the domain 
add new entry and paste the IP 

now all the traffic is on nginx port 80

so we need to create the reverse proxy 

sudo rm sudo vi /etc/nginx/nginx.conf //remove existing configurations 

sudo vi /etc/nginx/nginx.conf // add the below code 

events {
# Event directives...
http {
server {        //if want to add more servers copy form here 
listen 80;
server_name bel.100xdevs.com;
location
proxy_pass http://localhost:8080;
proxy_http_version 1.1;
proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
proxy_set_header Connection
'upgrade';
proxy_set_header Host Shost;
proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;
}
}
}

sudo nginx -s reload //restart the nginx

